  "label": "Legal Protection from Hate",
  "description": "The text references the idea of laws designed to prevent hatred or discrimination against certain groups. While such laws exist in many societies (e.g., hate crime statutes, anti-discrimination laws), the meme uses this concept ironically or cynically to suggest that some people are so 'disgusting' they need legal protection from being hated — a twisted inversion of the purpose of such laws.",
